          <p>
            That is a breakfast with as much protein as a chicken breast, plus fiber and slow-digesting carbohydrate, which makes protein oats a popular choice for lifters and for people trying to manage appetite. If you are eating for weight loss, watch the toppings; nut butter and sweeteners add calories fast. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-weight-loss/">best protein powder for weight loss</a> guide covers lower-calorie options.
          </p>

          <p>
            Protein needs vary by body size and goal, and our <a href="/how-much-protein-do-i-need/">how much protein do I need</a> guide covers daily targets. People with kidney disease, diabetes or other medical conditions should talk to a doctor or registered dietitian about protein and carbohydrate targets before making a high-protein breakfast a daily habit.
          </p>
